      "content": "wait, a goblin? lol. i know you're probably just making a joke, but it is a bit weird that you'd say that. \n\nthe sound is really specific though. it's not just a random noise; it's like this little scratching, almost like tiny claws on the metal, followed by that scurrying. if it's just sediment or a heating element, why would it sound so much like something is actually scurrying around in there? is there any mechanical reason why a part would make a sound that mimics something moving?",
